-- Passage rg8-character-setting-plot-p04
insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('1b0c7c86-144b-5240-8826-96be22cda1aa', 'rg8-character-setting-plot-p04', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-character-setting-plot'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Heron and the Beaver$q$, $q$A heron lived at the edge of a wide, slow river. Every morning she stood on one leg in the shallows and waited for fish. She was patient, and she was proud of it.

One summer, a young beaver began building a dam just upstream. He worked from dawn to dark, dragging branches and packing mud. The water near the heron's fishing spot grew deeper each day.

"You are ruining my shallows," the heron said. "Patient creatures do not rush about like you."

The beaver stopped, a stick still in his teeth. "I am not rushing," he said. "I am building a pond before the dry months come. Without it, there will be no water here at all by autumn."

The heron laughed. "The river has always been here. It will always be here." She turned her back and moved to a new spot downstream.

The beaver said nothing more. He went back to work.

By late August, no rain had fallen for six weeks. The river shrank to a thin brown thread. Downstream, the heron's new shallows turned to cracked mud, and the fish disappeared. At last, hungry and tired, she flew upstream.

There she found the beaver's pond, still full and cool. Fish moved in the deep water near the dam. The beaver sat on the bank and watched her land.

"You may fish here," he said. "There is enough."

The heron lowered her head. "I called you foolish for working hard," she said. "I mistook my stillness for wisdom."

Patience without foresight is only waiting.$q$, 'draft')
