  ('52cd3fe0-d993-575c-bd6c-15af9f571984', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-character-setting-plot'), null, 'hard',
   $q$Early in the story, Nadia practices only "with her bedroom door closed." What does her final request to Mr. Abernathy suggest about how the rehearsal changed her?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She still wants to make sure that no one ever hears her play.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"She is ready to practice the solo openly where she will perform it.","is_correct":true},{"text":"She plans to take the solo away from Jun-ho for the concert.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"She is upset with Mr. Abernathy and wants to avoid the class.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$She is ready to practice the solo openly where she will perform it.$q$, $q$Instead of hiding at home, she asks her teacher to let her practice in the rehearsal room, a step toward playing in front of others. Asking Mr. Abernathy directly shows she is not avoiding him or hiding her playing.$q$, 'draft', '4a4334d8-ca46-5e28-adc8-af833ef345d4')
