   $q$Which pattern of events do both texts share?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Three builders compete, and the fastest builder wins the contest.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"One builder fails three times and then gives up on the project.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-pattern"},{"text":"Two builders work together and share the credit for one bridge.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Three attempts are made, and the third succeeds after careful study.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Three attempts are made, and the third succeeds after careful study.$q$, $q$In both texts the first two bridges fail and the third works because someone studied first: the youngest brother watched the river, and Amara researched trusses. The fastest builders (the eldest brother and Dev) are the ones who fail, so speed does not win.$q$, 'draft', '470e60c2-9a22-544d-bada-45503f550c45')
