   $q$Which statement best describes how the author connects glaciers and rivers across the whole passage?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The author shows that the two are alike in every way except for how fast they move.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"},{"text":"The author traces how a glacier slowly melts and then turns into a river over time.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-sequence"},{"text":"The author shows shared traits, explains key differences, then places both in one larger system.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The author argues that glaciers matter more to the land than rivers do in most regions.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-purpose"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The author shows shared traits, explains key differences, then places both in one larger system.$q$, $q$The passage opens with similarities, then gives differences in how they move and how they shape valleys, and ends by calling both "moving parts of the water cycle." Speed is not the only difference, since paragraphs 3 and 4 add two more.$q$, 'draft', '8469820d-43cd-58be-a289-7f22795bd97b')
