   $q$Uncle Kenji says, "Time to replenish." Which meaning of "replenish" is supported by both the problem and the action in paragraph 5?$q$, $q$[{"text":"to clean something carefully","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"to close the shop for a break","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unrelated-meaning"},{"text":"to fill something up again","is_correct":true},{"text":"to sell everything that is left","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-cause-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$to fill something up again$q$, $q$The problem is shelves that are "almost bare," and the action is carrying trays "until every shelf was full again," so replenish means to fill up again. Selling the last rolls caused the empty shelves, so it is the cause of the problem, not the meaning of the word.$q$, 'draft', 'c77c3fe8-a781-573b-8959-df93d4610cf9')
