  ('cf1f918f-e99e-57ba-b1c3-d238f10cf960', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-evidence-inference'), null, 'medium',
   $q$The students noticed that more people walked on Birch Avenue during the hottest part of the day. What can most reasonably be inferred from this detail?$q$, $q$[{"text":"People likely chose the shaded street because it felt more comfortable.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Foundry Street was closed to walkers during the afternoon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"People in Marlow walk more in July than in any other month.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overgeneralization"},{"text":"Birch Avenue had more shops and restaurants than Foundry Street.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$People likely chose the shaded street because it felt more comfortable.$q$, $q$The passage links Birch Avenue's trees to sidewalks about twenty degrees cooler, so walkers probably preferred it in the heat. Nothing in the text mentions shops on either street, so that choice is not supported.$q$, 'draft', '4a9f1307-b21b-5181-b921-6c412b472af9')
