   $q$According to the passage, why did keepers clean the lens nearly every morning?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The burning fuel left black soot on the glass.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Salt air from the ocean rusted the glass overnight.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"confuses-detail"},{"text":"Fog and rain left the lens too wet to shine.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Inspectors came to check the lens every single day.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The burning fuel left black soot on the glass.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says the fuels "left black soot on the glass, so keepers cleaned the lens." Salt air is mentioned only as the reason keepers painted the tower.$q$, 'draft', '71b51725-6704-547c-8957-ff13f000b1a2')
