  ('732b8148-8ca0-5fd5-ac2e-920f78ea4267', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-evidence-inference'), null, 'easy',
   $q$According to the article, what did the science club find when it weighed the cafeteria trash?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Most of the food scraps were pieces of bread and rolls.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Twelve bags a day could have been recycled instead.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-number"},{"text":"About half of the trash, by weight, was food scraps.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Most of the trash, by weight, was plastic wrappers.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$About half of the trash, by weight, was food scraps.$q$, $q$The first paragraph says "about half of it, by weight, was food scraps." Twelve is the number of trash bags per day before the program, not a count of recyclable bags.$q$, 'draft', 'b05202f2-b3cd-56fa-8c59-0cb725edb085')
