   $q$Ms. Adebayo agreed to a trial if the club could show it "would not create a mess or attract pests." Which detail best shows the club addressed this concern?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Tomatoes and peppers from the garden ended up in the salad bar.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"},{"text":"The compost was kept in a fenced area and mixed with dry leaves to stop smells.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The cafeteria's trash bags dropped from twelve a day to seven by spring.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"supports-different-claim"},{"text":"The club is training sixth graders to take over the program.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"irrelevant-detail"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The compost was kept in a fenced area and mixed with dry leaves to stop smells.$q$, $q$A fence and a pile balanced with dry leaves so it does not smell answer the worry about mess and pests. The drop in trash bags shows the program reduced waste, which is a different point.$q$, 'draft', 'b05202f2-b3cd-56fa-8c59-0cb725edb085')
