  ('ab052208-f85f-56a8-883d-7691acb8e240', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-figurative-language'), null, 'easy',
   $q$Scientists call beavers "nature's engineers." What does this phrase mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Beavers fix broken machines that people leave outdoors.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Beavers build structures that change their surroundings.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Beavers have been trained by scientists to build things.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"Beavers are the only animals that can live near water.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Beavers build structures that change their surroundings.$q$, $q$Like human engineers, beavers design and build dams that reshape streams into ponds. The phrase is a metaphor, so it does not mean beavers were trained or work on machines.$q$, 'draft', '6bd74f3b-abac-5678-803e-68351084f0c7')
