   $q$The author says "busy as a beaver" now "sounds less like a complaint and more like praise." What change in meaning does the author describe?$q$, $q$[{"text":"\"Busy\" now means the beavers have stopped building dams.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"\"Busy\" now suggests useful work instead of annoying disruption.","is_correct":true},{"text":"\"Busy\" now describes the workers who install the pipes.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-referent"},{"text":"\"Busy\" now means beavers are harder to see than before.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$"Busy" now suggests useful work instead of annoying disruption.$q$, $q$Once communities manage the water, the beavers' constant building helps the wetland grow, so their busyness is seen as valuable. The passage says "The beavers keep working," so they have not stopped.$q$, 'draft', '6bd74f3b-abac-5678-803e-68351084f0c7')
