   $q$When the robot wanders into the hallway, Kenji says, "at least it knows how to make an exit." Why is this line funny?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Kenji is angry and wants the whole team to leave the room.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The phrase usually means leaving dramatically, and the robot literally left.","is_correct":true},{"text":"The robot made a sign that pointed everyone toward the door.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The robot was designed to find exits, so the test was a success.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The phrase usually means leaving dramatically, and the robot literally left.$q$, $q$"Make an exit" is a phrase for leaving in a noticeable way, and the broken robot really did roll out the door. Kenji is laughing, not angry, and the robot rolled off by accident.$q$, 'draft', '2d7f08c4-8dab-54c2-871c-7a3e1b97b79f')
