   $q$Mrs. Petrosyan says the pepper is "the most expensive pepper I have ever received. It cost you a whole summer." What does she mean?$q$, $q$[{"text":"She is jokingly saying that the pepper is small and worthless.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"false-irony"},{"text":"Darnell paid too much money for the pepper at a store.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"She is complaining that the pepper is not worth the compost.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-tone"},{"text":"The pepper is valuable because of the time and effort he put in.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The pepper is valuable because of the time and effort he put in.$q$, $q$She measures the pepper's cost in time, "a whole summer," which shows she values the work behind it. Darnell grows the pepper himself, so it was never bought, and his grin shows he takes her words as praise.$q$, 'draft', '5aeb9ff3-6716-500d-8fb7-b2db9eb52faf')
