   $q$Researchers believe monarchs "use the sun as a compass." What does this phrase suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Monarchs rest in the sunlight to warm their wings.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-comparison"},{"text":"Monarchs use the sun's position to tell which way to fly.","is_correct":true},{"text":"Monarchs fly only on days when the sun is very hot.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"Monarchs carry tiny compasses that point toward the sun.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Monarchs use the sun's position to tell which way to fly.$q$, $q$A compass shows direction, so the phrase means the sun guides the monarchs' direction. Resting in sunlight is something butterflies might do, but it has nothing to do with finding the way.$q$, 'draft', '89b4504f-6945-5d63-a6e0-b236c3d2ed1f')
