   $q$How does the opening sentence shape the reader's experience of the whole scene?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It reveals the secret at once, so the reader watches every near miss knowing what is at stake.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It hides the secret until the end, so the reader is surprised along with Coach Delgado.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"reverses-structure"},{"text":"It describes the families arriving, so the reader knows the party has already begun.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"It explains Coach's past seasons, so the scene becomes mostly a history of the team.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"too-narrow"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It reveals the secret at once, so the reader watches every near miss knowing what is at stake.$q$, $q$The first sentence tells the reader about the banner and who does not know about it, so Wren's excuses create suspense and humor. The secret is not hidden until the end; the reader learns it in the very first line.$q$, 'draft', '055b2607-5671-53ce-88c8-4e18850fa7f7')
