   $q$The final sentence says Coach smiled "a small smile that none of the runners noticed." How does this detail change what the reader knows?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It hints that Coach may have guessed the secret, which the runners do not realize.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It reveals that Tomasz told Coach about the banner earlier that afternoon.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It proves that Coach found the banner and has decided to skip the party.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"overstated-claim"},{"text":"It shows that the runners can now relax because the plan has fully worked.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misses-irony"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It hints that Coach may have guessed the secret, which the runners do not realize.$q$, $q$The smile hints that Coach may know more than she lets on, and the reader sees it while the runners do not, so now the runners are the ones left out. The detail only hints; it does not prove she found the banner or will skip the party.$q$, 'draft', '055b2607-5671-53ce-88c8-4e18850fa7f7')
