   $q$On Saturday the speaker sets an alarm and silences it "on the first note." What does this detail suggest?$q$, $q$[{"text":"The speaker must catch the bus early for a Saturday class.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"The speaker wants to sleep later than usual on the weekend.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"contradicts-text"},{"text":"The speaker finds the alarm annoying and wants it to stop.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"literal-reading"},{"text":"The speaker is choosing to follow the uncle's example and join his work.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$The speaker is choosing to follow the uncle's example and join his work.$q$, $q$The speaker repeats the uncle's exact habit from the first stanza and then walks with him to the shop, which shows the speaker is copying him on purpose. Getting up before dawn is the opposite of sleeping late.$q$, 'draft', '07fb6fed-7705-5e89-8bcd-aa3f85115900')
