insert into public.passages (id, code, skill_id, sat_alignment, grade_band, title, body, status)
values ('9877210d-25ae-55e9-8529-b62dfcfc2728', 'rg8-story-details-inference-p08', (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g8-story-details-inference'), null,
        '6-8', $q$The Kiln$q$, $q$When Ms. Ferreira opened the kiln on Thursday, the art room went quiet. Twenty-two bowls sat on the shelves in neat rows, glazed in blues and greens and one alarming orange. Twenty-one of them were whole.

Kofi's bowl had split clean in half.

He had spent three weeks on it. He had thrown it on the wheel, trimmed the base, and carved a ring of tiny leaves just under the rim. Ms. Ferreira had held it up in front of the class as an example of patient work. Now the two halves lay side by side like an open book.

"Air bubble," Ms. Ferreira said quietly, pointing to a small round hollow inside the break. "It happens to everyone. It happened to me last spring."

Kofi nodded. He did not trust his voice.

Around him, his classmates carried their bowls to their tables. Nadia, who sat next to him, looked from her own bowl to his and then set hers down on the far side of her backpack, where he could not see it.

At the end of class, Kofi did not throw the halves away. He wrapped them in a paper towel and put them in his locker. The next week, he came in early and asked Ms. Ferreira to show him how she wedged her clay, pressing and folding it on the table until it was smooth all the way through.

She showed him twice. He did it a third time on his own.$q$, 'draft')
